<title>UK: UK manufacturing up 0.6% in April.</title>
<headline>UK manufacturing up 0.6% in April.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics (ONS) released the following seasonally adjusted data on UK industrial production in April:</p>
<p>    MANUFACTURING OUTPUT	    APRIL   MARCH    (PREL MAR)</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change	    0.6    -0.1	(-0.1)</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change		2.3     1.2	 (1.4)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		 0.7     0.4	 (0.6)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change    1.7     1.4	 (1.6)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		103.7    103.1    (103.2)</p>
<p>INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change in pct   1.2    -0.2	(-0.1)</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change		2.2     0.2	 (0.5)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		-0.3    -0.2	 (0.1)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change    1.2     1.1	 (1.4)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		108.7   107.4     (107.8)</p>
<p>MINING/QUARRYING INCLUDING OIL AND GAS EXTRACTION</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change	    3.0    -0.6	 (0.3)</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change		1.8    -1.4	 (0.2)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		-3.2    -2.3	(-1.3)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change    0.5     1.1	 (2.2)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		144.8   140.6     (142.8)</p>
<p>ELECTRICITY, GAS AND WATER</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change	    4.5    -0.6	(-0.6)</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change		2.4    -6.4	(-6.3)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		-4.9    -3.0	(-2.7)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change   -2.4    -1.4	(-1.2)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		123.3   118.0     (118.1)</p>
<p>OIL AND GAS EXTRACTION</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		 4.0    N/A	 (-1.6)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change    1.3    N/A	  (3.5)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		179.6  174.5	(177.6)</p>
<p>NOTE - Consensus forecast was for industrial production to rise by 0.3 percent in April, for a year-on-year rise of 1.6 percent. Manufacturing output was expected to rise 0.3 percent on the month and 2.0 percent year-on-year.</p>
</text>
